# Bravo Healthcare — Architecture

Keep company facts in data files. Do not hard-code services, counties, nav, or contact info across pages.

- `src/data/company.ts`
- `src/data/navigation.ts`
- `src/data/services.ts` — `Service` type with slug, title, short/full description, icon, features, category, optional availabilityDisclaimer
- `src/data/counties.ts` — only the 15 approved Texas HHSC Region 6 counties

Reusable components: UtilityBar, Header, DesktopNavigation, MobileNavigation, Footer, HeroSection, SectionHeading, ServiceCard, ServiceGrid, CTASection, ContactForm, ReferralForm, CountyGrid, Breadcrumb, ResidentialComingSoon, EmergencyNotice, MissionSection, InsuranceNotice, ImageTextSection.

Prefer extending existing section components over creating page-specific duplicates.

Code quality: TypeScript, no `any`, server components by default, client components only for interaction. Use `next/image`. Accessible labels, visible focus, skip-to-content. No giant components or duplicate markup.

Service availability always depends on assessed needs, physician orders, eligibility, authorization, and approved service categories. Therapy: “When authorized and available.”
